index d53ebb88..bb3dc41d 100644
--- a/state/STATE.md
+++ b/state/STATE.md
@@ -1521,3 +1521,66 @@ exploratory simulation only. Real-data work must carry its own audited
 data and provenance and pass the leakage and perturbation gates before
 admission to the evidence base.
 
+---
+
+## Current activation (momentum cost-sensitivity + signal-definition defect — R-001, activation 45849553653, campaign slot 02)
+
+Bounded cost-sensitivity check for lookback 3/5/10 momentum under the
+repository's existing realistic cost model and a cost-matched coin-flip null.
+New artifacts: `research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` (check),
+`research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` (independent verifier),
+`state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json` (artifact).
+
+Method (predeclared, not tuned): existing 10-ticker universe; existing
+`bt.momentum_signals` (lookbacks 3/5/10); existing `bt.stress_segments`
+walk-forward regime gate (train=252d/test=84d/warmup=60d/overlap=60d, 4
+contiguous volatility blocks, min 400 bars/segment); matched null =
+framework `noise_benchmark` run with the SAME cost config on the same
+segments. Cost grid: zero / realistic (commission_per_trade=2.0,
+commission_per_share=0.003, slippage_cents=2.0, slippage_proportional=0.0005,
+the existing `examples/ma_crossover_real_data.py` model) / double (2x
+realistic).
+
+A-priori prediction (declared before execution): most zero-cost EDGE cells
+would fall to non-EDGE at the realistic level (COST_FRAGILE), because a daily
+rebalanced rule pays costs on nearly every bar. This prediction was
+**FALSIFIED**: 16/30 cells COST_ROBUST, 1/30 COST_FRAGILE, 13/30 NO_EDGE;
+6/10 assets COST_ROBUST overall (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA), 4/10
+NO_EDGE (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM). Cells EDGE: 17/30 zero, 18/30 realistic, 18/30
+double.
+
+Root cause of the falsification (verified finding): the existing
+`bt.momentum_signals` is **degenerate**. It computes
+`ret = mean(log(closes[i-lookback+1:i+1]))` — the mean of log PRICES, not the
+log return — which is > 0 for every price > 1, so the weight is +1 on
+4460/4465 bars for 9/10 assets (frac_long = 1.000). The "momentum" signal is
+therefore a near-constant LONG (constant-dollar) position, not a short-horizon
+direction bet; the falsified reversal class is the same construction with the
+opposite sign (near-constant short). This also explains the durable -0.99
+momentum/reversal P&L correlation: it is long-vs-short the same market, not a
+momentum/reversal signal pair. Only NVDA has a genuine long/short mix
+(frac_long 0.585 / frac_short 0.415, because its adjusted close was < 1 in the
+early window) and it is the only asset that shows material cost sensitivity:
+medians -0.038 (zero) -> -0.064 (realistic) -> -0.088 (double). The cost
+classification therefore describes the cost robustness of a constant-long
+position (low turnover, ~0.002 log-return cost per fold), NOT of a momentum
+strategy.
+
+Verification: preflight PASSED; leakage PASS (AMZN/JPM); independent verifier
+all gates MATCH — Gate 0 signal weight recount (9/10 always-long) MATCH; Gate 1
+fresh `walk_forward` + `noise_benchmark` recomputation (AMZN/JPM x lookbacks
+3/5/10 x zero/realistic/double) MATCH; Gate 2 zero-cost column cross-checks
+exactly against `momentum_results.json` and
+`momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json`; Gate 3 cost-robustness classification
+reproduces for all 10 tickers; determinism identical. Regression suite: 168
+tests OK.
+
+Decision: UNVERIFIED for the primary question (cost robustness of a genuine
+short-horizon momentum signal is not established, because the tested signal is
+degenerate). The verified durable finding is the signal-definition defect, which
+redirects the frontier: repair `momentum_signals` to use the actual log return
+(`log(close_t/close_{t-lookback})`) and re-register the momentum admission and
+cost test a-priori. The degenerate signal is a research finding, not a tool
+failure; fixing the signal rule is out of scope for this activation (it would be
+changing the signal after seeing results) and is handed off as a candidate task.
+
